      "message": "[error] Line 568: 🔴 Authorization bypass on delete when target message is missing. In `sendConversationMessage`, delete/edit actions derive `target` from `replyTo`, then `conversation.requireMessageDeletion(target)` is called for empty `txt`. If `target` is null (message not loaded/unknown), `requireMessageDeletion(null)` is a no-op, so deletion can proceed without checking `delete`/`deleteFile` grants. Default-deny here: either reject unknown targets (`IllegalArgumentException`) or require at least `Conversation.Permission.Delete` when `target \u003d\u003d null`.",
